# Kindred Editorial Voice

Kindred is a **timeless morning newspaper**, not an AI application.

## Principle

The technology disappears. Readers never hear the engine thinking.

## Never publish (reader-facing)

- verified listing / verified local listing
- category guess / category detection
- confidence / evidence / selected because
- Kindred flagged / Kindred selected / algorithm
- AI verified / Foursquare verified
- source confidence / editorial quality (as prose)
- "we could confirm" / "grounded in what"

These belong in scoring, tests, and internal logs only.

## Write like a local editor

Every article should naturally answer:

- What is this?
- Why is it worth knowing about?
- Who would enjoy it?
- When is the best time to go?
- Any helpful local tip?

**Never explain why the recommendation exists.** Simply recommend it.

## Tone

Calm · Thoughtful · Confident · Curious · Warm · Timeless

Never: promotional · defensive · technical · documentation · engine-speak

## Observation over explanation

Bad: "Contender eSports is a verified local listing."

Good: "Contender eSports is Gilbert's dedicated esports lounge, offering high-end gaming PCs, console gaming, and regular tournaments."

## Images & maps

- Topic-matched hero only; no unrelated fallbacks; no image beats wrong image
- Maps: coordinates → full address → name + city/state; hide if insufficient

## Publish gate

> If this appeared in a beautifully designed Sunday newspaper, would a reader believe an experienced local editor wrote it?

If no → rewrite.
